{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2","c3"],"primary":"c2","title":"New Jersey Anti-Eviction Act (good cause eviction)","requirement":"A residential landlord may evict a tenant or refuse to renew a lease only for a statutory good cause, through a court order, and after any required written Notice to Quit or Notice to Cease. Expiry of the lease term is not by itself a ground for eviction, and self-help evictions and lockouts are illegal.","key_value":"Good cause required to evict or refuse renewal; Notice to Quit periods range from 3 days to 3 years depending on cause; relocation assistance of 6x monthly rent for illegal-occupancy evictions","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1 et seq.","coverage_conditions":"Applies to most residential rental properties, including single-family homes, mobile homes and mobile home park land, apartment buildings and complexes, and rooming and boarding homes. Owner-occupied two- and three-family dwellings are subject to a separate, shorter list of causes.","exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises with two or fewer rental units (two- or three-unit owner-occupied buildings). Hotel or motel guests, and guest houses rented to transient or seasonal guests; hotel and motel occupants who reside there continually with no alternate residence are covered. A unit held in trust for a developmentally disabled immediate family member who permanently occupies it.","coverage_from":"c2","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c4"],"primary":"c4","title":"Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act (condominium/cooperative conversion) and Tenant Protection Act of 1992 (Hudson County)","requirement":"Eligible senior, disabled or disabled-veteran tenants in a building being converted to a condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership may be protected from eviction for up to 40 years if they apply, generally within 60 days. The 1992 Tenant Protection Act extends these protections to qualified tenants in Hudson County.","key_value":"40 years protected tenancy; 60-day application window; income limit is the greater of 3x average per-person county income or $50,000","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.22 to -61.39","coverage_conditions":"Buildings converted or being converted to a condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership. Covers qualified tenants only: age 62+ before the conversion recording date, permanently disabled, or honorably discharged and 60%+ service-disabled. The tenant must have lived in the building at least 1 year before the conversion recording date and must meet the income limit. The 1992 Act applies only in Hudson County.","exemptions":null,"coverage_from":"c4","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
